# G1 — Pages serves these with `s-maxage=604800` by default, so when the rename took
# `data-alex.enc` out of the build, Cloudflare's edge kept answering the old name with real
# ciphertext for the rest of that week: the deployment was clean and the leaking URL was not.
# Revalidation makes a blob that leaves the tree stop being served with it. Nothing loses a cache
# that matters — the app reads /api/vault/{id}, and these are only the seed path's fallback
# (functions/api/vault/[id].ts).
/data*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
